+    ///
+    /// The search starts at each root and follows child keys (through embedded children). It
+    /// collects every object it reaches that is pending creation (cached since the last time it
+    /// was written, in any `Create` state), and stops at objects that are stored: those read from
+    /// the database or the [`NodeSource`], those taken by an earlier call, and keys not in memory
+    /// (under the arena's invariants, a key referenced by an object in memory and not itself in
+    /// memory is stored). The collected objects become stored (`Read`) objects. Pending objects
+    /// that no root reaches stay pending, so they are collected later if a root reaches them.
+    ///
+    /// The caller keeps the GC-root counts itself: pending reference-count and root-count changes
+    /// of stored objects are discarded, as under `layout-v2` they only matter to this back-end's
+    /// own GC, which is not used together with this method.
